  "result": "The `drv.motion.halted` concept passed the gate (`OK`) on the first of six runs.\n\n**The concept:** the body says the road user's speed is at or below `speed_floor` at the observation:\n`.cmp (.measure \"kin_speed\" [aX]) .le pSpeedFloor`. There's no time operator around it because the contract sets no minimum duration. When the speed isn't observed, the result is unknown. The contract left nothing open, so I declared no narrowings.\n\n**The witnesses:** one instance with `speed_floor` set to 0.1 m/s. The road user is track 1, a motor vehicle heading east, and each trace has three observations 1 s apart.\n- **holds:** the vehicle stands at (0, 0) at 0 m/s, which gives compliant.\n- **fails:** the vehicle drives east at 4 m/s, which gives violated.\n- **blind:** the vehicle stands still but its speed is never set, and the manifest leaves out `kin.speed`, which gives unknown.\n\nThe record had no problems, so I didn't write a defect report. Everything is in `task_result.md` in the working directory.\n\nFiles changed:\n- `/local-scratch2/sma407/smoke31-run/pipeline/traffic-spec-agent/library/TrafficSpec/Concepts/motion/halted.lean`\n- `/local-scratch2/sma407/smoke31-run/pipeline/traffic-spec-agent/library/TrafficSpecWitness/Concepts/motion/halted.lean`",
